Continues the 2026-08-08 adversarial live-agent review fix pass.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6228 (Gaps findings 4/5/6/7), all in
scripts/kaggle/submission_kernel/main.py:

Gap 4: the swarm subprocess timeout equalled the full 12h Kaggle cap,
TimeoutExpired uncaught, return code never inspected, terminal "complete"
line unconditional -- a run that died at the deadline was a hard kill or
uncaught traceback, indistinguishable in the log from a crash at t=0.
Fixed: timeout=41400 (30 min margin), try/except TimeoutExpired, explicit
SWARM EXITED rc=N / SWARM TIMED OUT prints either way.

Gap 5: MAX_ACTIONS=2000 is sized on an unconfirmed 16 GiB host-RAM
assumption with no preflight to confirm it. Fixed: a /proc/meminfo
MemTotal print next to the existing nvidia-smi preflight line inside
AGENT_SRC. Also corrects (dated note, not silent edit) that block's own
stale "n_ctx 81920 / ~25.2 GB" illustrative example, now out of date
after REQ-ARC-WMTE-6227's re-measurement -- the live print was never
stale, only the prose example.

Gap 6: the agent-code self-locate was a bare next() over an rglob -- a
missing/re-laid-out dataset raised a message-free StopIteration at
import time, killing the run before any game while the kernel still
printed "complete". Fixed: list() the hits, print a loud
attach-the-dataset line, raise SystemExit instead of a bare
StopIteration.

Gap 7: the agent's llama-server stderr log landed in /tmp inside the
ephemeral Kaggle container -- the only discriminator between a
recoverable context-overflow and a server death via ggml_abort, gone the
moment the run ends. Fixed: os.environ.setdefault("CARNOT_ARC_SERVER_LOG_DIR",
"/kaggle/working") at the top of the outer script, before run_env's
os.environ.copy(), so child processes inherit it.

Tests: test_arc_kaggle_kernel_gaps_20260808.py (10 tests), using the same
source-slice-and-exec() pattern as the existing
test_arc_kernel_agent_src_executable.py -- exercises the actual shipped
statements, not a re-typed copy. Broader sweep: 32 passed across the
kernel/generator-pin/submission-readiness test files.

Also acknowledges 1 results/ artifact flagged stale by the artifact-
freshness-lint: its own scripts never import or execute the kernel file,
only name it in descriptive prose about a historical (2026-07-27) build
session.

Committed via pathspec (not git add -A): the conductor is concurrently
mid-commit on its own REQ-ARC-WMTE-6213 work in the same working tree
(files already staged in the index), and this commit must not sweep that
up -- verified after the fact that the conductor's staged files are
